E='IV. Reused typescripts: separate questions, scope tests and source dependencies'
add('N48',E,'Coxeter realizability is deferred beyond the necessary diagram restrictions','007,005,035','007:5–22; 005:continuation; 035:5','unproved claim',r'''The typescript says “il restera ensuite à voir que ces possibilités sont effectivement réalisées,” equivalently that the resulting Coxeter groups are finite or the quadratic form is positive nondegenerate. The lemma and valency/edge-order corollaries on 007–005 supply necessary restrictions, while the later root-system construction programme on 035 offers a realization route. This is a deferred step of the reused source, not a new conjecture inferred from the handwritten cohomology programme.''',C+' N43 (111,109,107,105,103,101) **differs** mathematically but similarly tracks a reused source in printed order; the present material **adds** a Coxeter-source dependency under register **MPL_33_098-146 §1/§65** (first-pass leads), with no matching result.',['Coxeter','quadratic','finite group','realiz','deferred'])
add('N49',E,'The type-A endpoint formula has a rank-one exception to test','013','4,10–18','own idea',r'''The heading includes “$(\ell\geq1)$,” while the final formula sets both endpoint pairings with the highest root equal to $1$. At $\ell=1$, the same sheet gives $\widetilde\alpha=\alpha_1=\varepsilon_1-\varepsilon_2$ and $\|\alpha_1\|^2=2$, so that pairing is $2$. This is an internal exceptional-rank check, leaving the source's intended exception and the frozen text separate.''',C+' N46 (105,109,111,131,135,139,143) contains **different** source anomalies; this **adds** a root-system collation question, with no same-point entry and only the reused-source lead **MPL_33_098-146 §1** in '+R+'.',['root','racine','endpoint','rank','A_'],'high for the substitution using the same sheet; no historical novelty or attribution is claimed')
add('N50',E,'Reducedness and irreducibility are expressly left for casewise verification','019,013,027,031','019:4–6; 013:6–14; 027/031:root constructions','self-flagged: a step the reused source itself marks as unverified',r'''“Il restera naturellement à vérifier dans chaque cas que le système $R$ est réduit et irréductible” follows the lattice-shell reflection argument. The type-$A$ construction on 013 explicitly addresses irreducibility, and the exceptional constructions supply further cases in the source's printed order, but the available leaves are not a complete verification of every announced type. The standing question should record both the deferred check and the partial internal continuation.''',C+' §VI, especially N55/S14 (145, a different reused source), **differs** in content; this **adds** a source-marked verification task under register **MPL_33_098-146 §65** (first-pass lead), without relating it to the LM4/LM7 open problems.',['irreduc','reduced','vérifier','verify','root'])
add('N51',E,'The ambiguous L3 generator has a mathematical consequence without deciding the ink','017','12','reading question',r'''The generator in the formula for “$L_3$” contains the frozen alternative $\xi_i\mid\varepsilon_i$, with the xi-like reading first. Nearby xi symbols denote coordinates and epsilon symbols basis vectors, so the first reading makes the displayed half-sum different in type from the expected vector generator. This is a priority for collation, not authority to select the expected alternative.''',C+' has no matching L3 or root-lattice passage; the lattice language in **WG H9** and **WG2 §2.1 #2** **differs** in subject, so this **adds** a reading question without changing those unchecked plan statuses.',['L_3','root','lattice','epsilon','xi'])
add('N52',E,'The connection-index calculation is taken up immediately','023','12','unproved claim',r'''The phrase “qu'il reste à calculer” introduces a quotient computation which the same paragraph then carries out using projected basis vectors and an order-three generator. It should be indexed as a calculation supplied in outline, not left on the list of unresolved authorial questions. A detailed check would verify the asserted generating set and the exact order, rather than treating the introductory future tense as evidence of abandonment.''',C+' N27 (132,134, trace-existence reduction subsequently addressed) **differs** mathematically but provides the same reporting distinction; the current paragraph **adds** a source-internal completion, with no root-system result in '+R+' and no change to its statuses.',['quotient','calcul','generator','order','completed'])
add('N53',E,'The E6 exponent product is arithmetically inconsistent as written','023','18–23','own idea',r'''The factor “$(12+1)$” makes the left side of the exponent-product equation divisible by $13$ for integral $m,m'$, whereas its right side $51{,}840$ has remainder $9$ modulo $13$. The preceding exponent list contains $11$, giving a specific internal collation lead without deciding where the discrepancy arose. The literal $12$ remains in the frozen transcription.''',C+' N46 (105,109,111,131,135,139,143) has **different** reused-source anomalies; this **adds** an arithmetic check, not a contradiction of an earlier established result, with register **MPL_33_098-146 §1** only a first-pass source-accounting lead.',['E_6','exponent','51','root','arithmetic'],'high: divisibility alone contradicts the displayed equation, independently of any published root table')
add('N54',E,'An ordered B2 root pair tests the stated ratio and order rule','035','7','own idea',r'''The assertion that $n(u,v)=-1$ gives $\|v\|/\|u\|=1$ and order $3$ needs an ordering or equivalent qualification. In the reduced system $\{\pm e_1,\pm e_2,\pm e_1\pm e_2\}$, simple roots $u=e_1-e_2$ and $v=e_2$ give $n(u,v)=-1$, ratio $1/\sqrt2$, and $s_us_v$ a quarter-turn of order $4$. This tests the isolated ordered-pair wording even in an irreducible example; missing earlier conventions still have to be recovered.''',C+' N50–N51 (135) and N54 (145) provide **different** conditional algebraic scope tests; this **adds** a root-pair test, and register **MPL_33_098-146 N54** remains an unreviewed methodological parallel.',['root','norm','reflection','ratio','scope'],'high: both dot products and the two reflection matrices are explicit')
add('N55',E,'Global length labels need a scope convention for reducible systems','035,033','035:9; 033:11–13','own idea',r'''With the global minimum “$\lambda$” used on 035, the reduced system $\{\pm e_1,\pm2e_2\}$ has lengths $1$ and $2$, outside the three stated alternatives $\lambda,\lambda\sqrt2,\lambda\sqrt3$. This calls for an irreducibility or component-normalization convention before extending the definition to arbitrary reduced systems. Once the stated global weight function does exist, however, it records relative component scales, so the single rescaling factor on 033 is not itself a counterexample.''',C+' and '+R+' match “lattice” only to **WG H9** (cote 44, Theorems 4–5, no exact scan supplied) and **WG2 §2.1 #2** (another graded/symplectic-lattice programme): this **differs** from both unchecked plans and **adds** a source-specific scope test.',['lattice','root','reduc','scale','normaliz'],'high for the two-component example and the logical distinction; medium for the proposed missing-convention explanation')
add('N56',E,'The E8 dimension label conflicts with the surrounding coordinates','049','4–10','reading question',r'''Part (IV) explicitly uses $\mathrm R^8$, while (VI) writes “$V=\mathrm R^4$” in the same eight-coordinate calculation. This is an internal source discrepancy to collate, and the eight weights split between 049 and 037 make the intended ambient space a precise question. The frozen $4$ is not replaced by an expected $8$.''',C+' N46 (105,109,111,131,135,139,143) **differs** in its examples; this **adds** a dimension-label question to README **S19**, with no E8 result in '+R+' and only **MPL_33_098-146 §1** as unreviewed source context.',['E_8','dimension','coordinate','root','weight'])
add('N57',E,'The E8 highest-root pairing can be tested from these sheets alone','019,037,049','019:6; 037:18–23; 049:4–6','own idea',r'''The two weight displays on 037 give $\alpha_8=2\omega_8-\omega_7=\varepsilon_7-\varepsilon_6$, while $\widetilde\alpha=\omega_8=\varepsilon_7+\varepsilon_8$. With the orthonormal convention on 019, the pairing is $+1$, conflicting with the literal “$(\widetilde\alpha|\alpha_8)=-1$” on 049. This uses only the supplied formulas, not a published root table, and leaves the transcription unchanged.''',C+' N46 (105,109,111,131,135,139,143) gives **different** internal anomalies; this **adds** a pairing check, with no matching context scan or settled register result and **MPL_33_098-146 §1** remaining a source-accounting lead.',['highest','root','weight','pairing','orthogonal'],'high: subtracting the alpha-coefficient vectors leaves exactly alpha_8, and the epsilon dot product is immediate')
add('N58',E,'The E7 numeric doubts remain independent of mathematical expectation','029,031','029:41; 031:16','reading question',r'''The last epsilon index in the weight “$\omega_7$” on 029 is frozen as $8\mid6$, and an upper summation bound on 031 as $6\mid8$. These alternatives would change any consistency calculation using the formulas, so such calculations must state which branch they test. The later contextual reports contain no E7 parallel that can adjudicate the ink, and a familiar root realization cannot silently decide it.''',C+' N33 (138–142, interval-letter/indexing doubts) **differs** in subject; this **adds** a root-formula collation priority, with no matching entry in '+R+' and no change to any result status.',['E_7','index','bound','root','notation'])
add('N59',E,'The hyperalgebra question is editorial in a reused source','009','10','self-flagged: a step the reused source itself marks as unverified',r'''“On ne sait si l'on définira en général la notion d'hyperalgèbre” concerns whether the text will introduce the notion at that level of generality. It is an editorial uncertainty, not a demonstrated mathematical nonexistence claim. The surrounding page-edit instructions and the title “Variétés de groupe” should remain part of that source context rather than being attributed automatically to the handwritten cohomology programme.''',C+' N42/N56 (099,101–121,125–143) **restate** the need to separate reused-source identity and authorship; this **adds** another explicit uncertainty under register **MPL_33_098-146 §1/§65** (first-pass leads).',['hyper','formal group','group','editorial','reused'])
add('N60',E,'The formal-kernel sorites preserve a restricted final surjectivity','009','22–42','unproved claim',r'''“On pourrait donner les sorites suivants pour les noyaux formels” proposes the functorial and tangent-space properties of $\underline V(A)$. The final sequence has a dashed last arrow, qualified by finite dimension of $G$ or openness of $J$. A proof should recover the topologies and completion conventions behind these statements before promoting that conditional last surjectivity to an unconditional exact sequence.''',C+' N50–N51 (135, distinct completeness/coefficient-field issues) **differ** from these formal-group assertions; this **adds** a separate topological-algebra dependency to README **S19**, with no same-point result in '+R+'.',['formal','completion','topolog','surject','exact'])
add('N61',E,'The regular graded-algebra corollary depends on an unseen proposition','011','5–16','reading question',r'''The corollary begins “Si les conditions de la prop. 1 sont vérifiées” and uses the preceding implications and Tor localization to obtain regularity, generator-degree invariance and the Poincaré series. Its original Proposition 1 is not on this leaf, and the last sentence continues off the page after “(sans.” The conditional graded-ring result must not be applied to the later finite coefficient rings merely because both discussions use Tor.''',C+' N08/N25 (108,112,126–132) **differ** in their coefficient-ring setting, and N43 (111,109,107,105,103,101) and N45 (107,115,113) concern other reused algebraic dependencies; this **adds** a missing-hypothesis/source-continuation question under register **MPL_33_098-146 N08/N25** (first-pass leads).',['Tor','graded','regular','Poincar','algebra'])
add('N62',E,'The product restriction formula has a domain-index question','041','9','reading question',r'''The restriction equation uses the projection $\widetilde p_{xV}$ but says “where for $x\in U$,” although that projection belongs to the product indexed by $V$. A point of $U\setminus V$ exposes the literal domain problem. This is separate from the stronger Hom assertion on 043, and the frozen wording remains unchanged.''',C+' N18 (120, boundary stalks) and N31 (138,140, stalkwise bounds) **differ**; this **adds** an elementary projection-index issue to README **S19**, with no same-point result in '+R+'.',['stalk','projection','product','P_X','restriction'])
add('N63',E,'A two-point space tests the product-of-stalks Hom assertion','041,043','041:9; 043:5–9','own idea',r'''For the claim “It is easily checked that these maps are inverses,” take $X=\{a,b\}$ with opens $\varnothing,\{b\},X$ and, in $k$-vector spaces for a field $k$, the constant sheaf $F=F′$ with identity restriction. Then $P_XF(X)=k^2$, $P_XF(\{b\})=k$, restriction is the second projection, and $\varphi_X(s,t)=(t,0)$ with $\varphi_{\{b\}}=0$ is a sheaf morphism. The proposed extraction returns point maps $(\mathrm{id},0)$ and reconstructs $(s,t)\mapsto(s,0)$, so it does not recover $\varphi$. This refutes the literal assertion for general spaces while leaving open whether unseen earlier hypotheses restricted $X$.''',C+' N18 (120) and N31 (138,140) are **different** uses of stalks, and N54 (145) a different conditional counterexample; this **adds** a categorical scope test under register **MPL_33_098-146 N54** (unreviewed methodological lead), not a repetition of its étale-criterion example.',['P_X','stalk','Hom','product','sheaf'],'high: the only nontrivial restriction square commutes, and the two reconstructed maps differ explicitly')
add('N64',E,'The sheaf reflector theorem needs its categorical conventions recovered','045,039','045:11–29; 039:4–16','unproved claim',r'''“complete … and have enough small objects” and “right perfect” are explicit hypotheses of the reflector theorem, with definitions referred to Chapter I. Scan 039 starts the intersection-of-subsheaves construction and lists further consequences, but the argument continues beyond the surviving leaf. These dependencies should be recovered before comparing the theorem with a modern sheafification assertion for an arbitrary coefficient category; the concrete Hom failure on 043 does not by itself refute every consequence of the reflector theorem.''',C+' N06 (106, derived adjunction) **differs** despite shared injective language; this **adds** a distinct foundational source under register **MPL_33_098-146 §1** (first-pass source lead), with no matching theorem in '+R+'.',['reflect','small object','right perfect','sheaf','injective'])
add('N65',E,'The cancelled sheet leaves the arbitrary-n implication without separation open','047','6','self-flagged: a step the reused source itself marks as unverified',r'''The sheet says “Nous ignorons s'il en est encore ainsi (sans hypothèse de séparation) pour $n$ quelconque,” referring to b)$\Rightarrow$c), and separately says that c)$\Rightarrow$b) fails even for $n=1$. Conditions b) and c) are absent from this leaf, so their meaning cannot be reconstructed from the later section title alone. Whole-sheet cancellation records the state of the paper, not proof that the mathematical question was subsequently solved or withdrawn.''',C+' N55/S14 (145, another reused source with missing premises/proofs) **differs**; this **adds** a separate explicit unknown to register **MPL_33_098-146 §65** (first-pass standing-question lead), with no same-point result.',['separation','séparation','filtration','regular sequence','ignor'])
add('N66',E,'An elementary example separates the two filtrations on R','047','14–31','own idea',r'''For “les filtrations $(R''_k)$ et $(R'_k)$ sont en général distinctes,” take $A=k[t]$, $J=(t)$, $N=A$, $R=tA$, $M=k$, $N_0=A$ and $N_k=0$ for $k\geq1$. Direct substitution gives $N'_1=tA$, $R'_1=R\cap N'_1=tA$, and $R''_1=R_1+JR_0=t^2A$, with $R'_1/R''_1\cong k$. This makes the failure to commute modification with passage to a submodule concrete, without addressing the undefined b)$\Rightarrow$c) question.''',C+' N50–N51 (135) have **different** local-algebra scope examples; this **adds** a filtration example, with no same-object context scan or settled result and only **MPL_33_098-146 §1** as unreviewed source context.',['filtration','graded','submodule','regular sequence','Tor'],'high: the strict inclusion follows directly from the two definitions on the supplied sheet')
add('N67',E,'Paper reuse establishes several source strands, not one authorship','005–049 odd','printed headings and pagination','reading question',r'''The root/Coxeter pages, the “Variétés de groupe” editorial sheet, the graded-algebra fragment, the English sheaf-theory leaves and the cancelled filtered-module sheet form distinguishable typed strands. Printed pagination gives internal continuation orders, but neither adjacency nor mathematical familiarity identifies one author or links all their claims to Grothendieck's handwritten programme. Their questions and anomalies are therefore indexed as reused-source material throughout these notes.''',C+' scope §1, N42/N56 and T07/T08 (099,101–145 odd) **restate** this provenance caution; the present scans **add** new observed strands and pagination under register **MPL_33_098-146 §1**, an unreviewed source-accounting lead.',['reused','typescript','authorship','pagination','source'])
add('N68',E,'The Coxeter-to-Dynkin ambiguity is deferred exposition','021','6–8','unproved claim',r'''“On verra par contre ci-dessous” promises the distinction between a Coxeter diagram and the possible weighted Dynkin diagrams, before the irreducible classification theorem and its first drawings. The weights and the different lower-rank restrictions on the displayed B and C families are part of that source-specific convention. A complete check must recover the intended irreducible scope and the missing continuation rather than infer a new classification claim from this single leaf.''',C+' N43 (111–101, another reused argument with internal continuations) **differs** mathematically; this **adds** a classification-source dependency under register **MPL_33_098-146 §1/§65** (first-pass leads), with no Coxeter/Dynkin result in '+R+'.',['Coxeter','Dynkin','classification','below','deferred'])
save_manifest()

T='VI. Standing question: title sheets, internal titles and page counts'
add('T01',T,'The global-duality title sheet','046','2–5','reading question',r'''The title-only sheet reads “19) Le th de dualité globale : énoncé général pour un morphisme lisse compactifiable” and carries the small folio 45. It is an actual title sheet in this package, but gives no total page count and contains no statement or proof of the announced theorem.''',C+' T01/T02 (098–146, no cover in that package) **differs** in the presence of a cover here; this **adds** a title-sheet observation under register **MPL_33_098-146 §1/§65**, with no claim about date or completion.',['title','cover','dualité','global','page count'])
add('T02',T,'Observed package size and source composition','002–049','all pages; inventory','reading question',r'''The supplied run contains 48 scans, with inventory classifications of 24 text sheets, 23 reused typed sheets and one cover. Titles such as “Variétés de groupe” and the English “1.4 Theorem” identify distinct inserted source strands, while the cancellation on 047 does not establish that it is Grothendieck's own draft. These are counts of this supplied package, not a manuscript declaration of a 48-page work.''',C+' T01 (098–146: 49 scans, 25 handwritten and 24 reused typed) **differs** in its observed counts; the present inventory **adds** a separately bounded package under register **MPL_33_098-146 §1**, without turning either package boundary into a work boundary.',['48','49','count','handwritten','reused','cover'])
add('T03',T,'Folio numbers, section numbers and pagination are separate sequences','002–049','folio markers and headings','reading question',r'''The small folio sequence on these scans is 1–48, with folio number equal to scan number minus one; source pagination and other numbers coexist with it. The circled “15” on 022 belongs with “Classe fondamentale locale,” while the frozen section number on 032 remains $16\mid15$. No explicit total such as “19 pages” or a declared range such as “Pages 1–67” occurs in this package.''',C+' T02–T06 (098–146, including circled 26/30/31/32 on 100–146) **restate** the need to separate number systems and **differ** in their actual numbers; this **adds** current sequence data under register **MPL_33_098-146 §1/§65**.',['folio','circled','page count','numbering','pages'])
add('T04',T,'The handwritten outline has cancellations and restarts','002,004,006,010,012,014,016,018,022,026,032,034,036,038,046,048','headings; table below','reading question',r'''The outline runs from “Site étale” through supports, purity, fundamental classes and derived categories to “20) Exemple,” with the explicit titles indexed below. Cancelled headings on 014 and 034, the uncertain $16\mid15$ on 032 and the restarted items 18 and 19 are evidence of drafting, not permission to impose a new continuous numbering. The scope reaches a global-duality title and examples, without establishing that this set of leaves is a finished chapter.''',C+' T03–T06 (100–146, “Formulaire” and later Lefschetz/Verdier titles) **adds** a concrete continuation/comparison target but **differs** in its numbering and local headings; bears on register **MPL_33_098-146 N41** as a first-pass formalism lead, not a dating result.',['Formulaire','title','Lefschetz','Verdier','numbering','duality'])
add('T05',T,'The numbered French typescripts have their own discontinuous pagination','005,007,011,013,015,017,019,021,023,025,027,029,031,033,035,037,049','printed headings and page numbers','reading question',r'''The leaves marked “n° 391” carry the printed pages recorded below, including the separate graded-algebra fragment on 011 and the root-system titles on 013, 027 and 031. Those titles are “5. Systèmes de type $A_\ell$,” “12. Système de type $E_6$” and “11. Système de type $E_7$.” The counts and references to numbered planches within this source are not a total page count for cote 33 or evidence that the sources share one author.''',C+' T07/T08 (099–145 odd, different printed page sequences) **restate** the source-pagination problem and **differ** in the material identified; this **adds** another source inventory under register **MPL_33_098-146 §1**, with no root-system theorem supplied by '+R+'.',['typescript','pagination','printed','planch','source','page'])
add('T06',T,'The group-varieties sheet is an editorial page, not a page-count cover','009','2–4,10–42','reading question',r'''“Variétés de groupe,” printed “- 22 -” and the margin “Tribu n° 62” identify the observed sheet. Its references to P. 3-13, P. 3-14 and P. 3-15 à 3-19 are editorial cross-references, not a declaration of the number of pages supplied here. They should guide source collation without assigning an author from the reuse alone.''',C+' N56/T07/T08 (101–145 odd) **restate** the need for source identification and **differ** in the observed headings; this **adds** a bibliographic lead under register **MPL_33_098-146 §1**, with no exact same-source match supplied.',['Tribu','Variétés','group','editorial','printed','authorship'])
add('T07',T,'The English sheaf-theory pages occur out of source order','039,041,043,045','source page numbers; 045:12','reading question',r'''The English sheets have source pages 40, 34, 38 and 39 at scans 039, 041, 043 and 045 respectively. “1.4 Theorem” begins on source page 39, with its consequences and proof on page 40, so the order 041→043→045→039 supplies a partial reconstruction with source pages 35–37 absent from this package. None is a title sheet or a declaration of total extent.''',C+' T07/T08 (099–145 odd) **differs** in source and pagination; this **adds** an internally ordered sheaf-theory strand under register **MPL_33_098-146 §1**, without identifying it with the earlier operator-algebra leaf on 099.',['sheaf','page','pagination','source','Theorem'])
add('T08',T,'The cancelled filtered-module sheet retains a section title and source page','047','2–10','reading question',r'''The entirely cancelled typescript carries source page “IV-1007” and “19.6. Suites régulières relativement à un module,” with “quotient” deleted and “filtré” inserted. The small folio 46 belongs to the package sequence; IV-1007 is source pagination and is not a claim that this package contains 1007 pages. The title's alteration and whole-sheet cancellation do not establish the disposition of its explicit unknown b)$\Rightarrow$c).''',C+' N55/T08 (145, a different incomplete reused source) **differs**; this **adds** a cancelled source-title observation under register **MPL_33_098-146 §1/§65**, with no same-point result in '+R+'.',['filtr','regular','cancel','title','page','separation'])
save_manifest()

add('N69',A,'The cancelled analytic-local argument is replaced by a proof request','006,008','006:30; 008:2–19','withdrawn in the same text: 006 → 008',r'''The cancelled “Remarque” about a proper scheme over an analytic local ring on 006 is followed by a cancelled “On peut … montrer que” neighborhood-limit formula on 008. The live text then starts a relative algebraic/analytic comparison and explicitly asks for its isomorphism proof. This is a withdrawal of that presentation and a restart of the argument, not evidence that the underlying continuity or comparison assertion was disproved.''',C+' N36 (144,146, another cancelled construction followed by a restart) **differs** in the actual pairing and **restates** the need to preserve draft state; this **adds** a two-scan revision under register **MPL_33_098-146 §65/N36**, without identifying the mathematical questions.',['analytic','limit','cancel','restart','withdraw'])
save_manifest()

add('N70',E,'The promised eight cases and nine plates are only partially present','017,015,013,027,031','017:16; 015:4–26; type headings','unproved claim',r'''“Nous allons voir successivement” on 017 promises constructions in the next eight numbered sections, and 015 says the eleven kinds of data “seront rassemblées dans les planches II à X” for nine types. The supplied type-A, E7 and E6 headings and other continuation leaves realize part of that exposition, but the promised complete plate collection is not in this package. This is a source-continuation task, distinct from the narrower deferred reducedness/irreducibility check and from a declaration of page count.''',C+' N43/T07 (111–101 and other reused source pagination) **differs** in subject but supplies a **related** source-continuation problem; this **adds** a specific plate promise under register **MPL_33_098-146 §1/§65**, with no root-table result in '+R+'.',['planch','eight','nine','source','continuation','pagination'])
add('N71',A,'The support exact and spectral sequences are left as headings','012','23–41','unproved claim',r'''After identifying local cohomology with Ext and recording the low-degree kernel/cokernel description, the page ends this part with bare “Suite” and the alternatives “exacte” and “spectrale.....” The actual sequences and their connecting maps are not written there. A reconstruction should specify the support and open-immersion derived functors before comparing their edge maps with the cycle-class construction, rather than treating the headings as a completed proof.''',C+' N01 (098, closed-immersion duality) **adds a later formalism lead**, while N05 (104, hyper-Tor) **differs** in the spectral sequence involved; this **adds** an explicit unfinished display to register **MPL_33_098-146 N01/§65** (first-pass leads).',['support','Ext','spectral','sequence','closed','immersion'])
add('N72',B,'The base-change proof indication leaves its reduction unstated','012,014','012:44–57; 014:16','unproved claim',r'''“Dém presque immédiate par th. de changement de base......” is the only proof indication at the end of the twist discussion following the purity statement. It does not specify the local model, the reduction, or which base-change theorem is used. Recovering that intended argument should retain the prime-to-residual-characteristic hypothesis and should not turn this compressed indication into a proof of the separately boxed absolute-purity problem.''',C+' N12 (114, comparison functoriality) and N20 (122, resolution-free curve expectation) **differ** in object; this **adds** a proof-reconstruction task to README **S19** and register **MPL_33_098-146 §65**, without a same-point settled result.',['pureté','purity','base change','changement de base','proof','résolution'])

# Expand composite register labels into the exact IDs supplied by the register.
def expand_register(m):
 ids=re.findall(r'(?:N\d+|§\d+)',m.group(1))
 if len(ids)<2:return m.group(0)
 return ' and '.join('**MPL_33_098-146 '+i+'**' for i in ids)
for note in NOTES:
 note['comparison']=re.sub(r'\*\*MPL_33_098-146 ([^*]+)\*\*',expand_register,note['comparison'])
save_manifest()

# Search every supplied context file for every final note; do not truncate hits.
context_files=sorted(p.relative_to(CTX).as_posix() for p in CTX.rglob('*') if p.is_file())
assert context_files==['README.md','notes/RESULTS_STATE.md','same_cote_33/MPL_33_098-146_notes.md']
import hashlib
searches={
 'method':'rg --json --ignore-case --fixed-strings; multiple literal terms combined by OR; all supplied context files; all matching lines retained',
 'context_files':[{'path':f,'sha256':hashlib.sha256((CTX/f).read_bytes()).hexdigest()} for f in context_files],
 'notes':[]
}
summary=['# Per-note context search index','',
 'Each row searches all three supplied context files. Counts are matching lines, not claims of mathematical equivalence; the note comparison supplies that assessment. The JSON record retains queries, all hits, and zero-hit files.','',
 '| Item | Literal search terms | README hits | Results-register hits | Same-cote-note hits |',
 '|---|---|---|---|---|']
for note in NOTES:
 args=['rg','--json','--ignore-case','--fixed-strings']
 for term in note['terms']:args.extend(['-e',term])
 result=subprocess.run(args+context_files,cwd=CTX,text=True,capture_output=True)
 assert result.returncode in (0,1),(note['id'],result.stderr)
 per_file={f:[] for f in context_files}
 for line in result.stdout.splitlines():
  entry=json.loads(line)
  if entry['type']!='match':continue
  d=entry['data'];path=d['path']['text']
  per_file[path].append({'line':d['line_number'],'text':d['lines']['text'].rstrip('\n')})
 searches['notes'].append({'id':note['id'],'terms':note['terms'],
  'files':[{'path':f,'match_count':len(per_file[f]),'matches':per_file[f]} for f in context_files]})
 counts=[str(len(per_file[f])) for f in context_files]
 terms=', '.join(note['terms']).replace('|','\\|')
 summary.append('| '+note['id']+' | '+terms+' | '+' | '.join(counts)+' |')
(ROOT/'records/context_search.json').write_text(json.dumps(searches,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
(ROOT/'records/context_search_summary.md').write_text('\n'.join(summary)+'\n')

# Render the complete principal research-note file, grouping stable IDs by subject.
def render_note(note):
 s=[f"### {note['id']}. {note['title']}",'',
  f"**File:** cote 33. **Scan(s):** {note['scans']}. **Approx. TeX line(s):** {note['lines']}. **Kind:** {note['kind']}.",'',
  note['body'],'',f"**Context / register comparison:** {note['comparison']}"]
 if note['confidence']:s.extend(['',f"**Own-idea confidence and reason:** {note['confidence']}."])
 s.extend(['',f"**Context search:** {note['id']} in `records/context_search.json` (all three supplied files).",''])
 return '\n'.join(s)

out=[(ROOT/'records/notes_frontmatter.md').read_text().rstrip(),'']
for section in (A,B,D,E):
 out.extend(['## '+section,''])
 out.extend(render_note(note) for note in NOTES if note['section']==section)
out.append((ROOT/'records/standing_steps.md').read_text().rstrip())
out.extend(['','## '+T,''])
out.extend(render_note(note) for note in NOTES if note['section']==T)
for name in ('title_pagination_tables.md','register_disposition.md','primary_comparisons.md'):
 out.extend(['',(ROOT/'records'/name).read_text().rstrip()])
(ROOT/'MPL_33_002-049_notes.md').write_text('\n'.join(out)+'\n')
assert len(NOTES)==len({n['id'] for n in NOTES})
print(json.dumps({'notes':len(NOTES),'research_items':sum(n['id'].startswith('N') for n in NOTES),
 'title_items':sum(n['id'].startswith('T') for n in NOTES),'context_files_searched_per_note':len(context_files),
 'notes_bytes':(ROOT/'MPL_33_002-049_notes.md').stat().st_size,'search_bytes':(ROOT/'records/context_search.json').stat().st_size},indent=2))
